{"attachments":[{"content_type":"image/png","filename":"SabrineLovlatar.png","id":"863478232925077513","local_path":"discord/empire-city/attachments/850808447003656242/863478232925077513-SabrineLovlatar.png","message_id":"863478232452300811","sha256":"c163b4be5625ab1a8f813f61e5258b28515f4c7348cd1105d639514ab4f984ca","size":363822,"url":"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/850808447003656242/863478232925077513/SabrineLovlatar.png?ex=6ac09885&is=6abf4705&hm=95068a018d1bc297eee4d2066bceab8fd391415f5f51af55f88ba1f8a4631d06&"}],"author":{"display_name":"Cruithne","id":"150319814836092928","is_bot":0,"username":"cruithne"},"author_id":"150319814836092928","channel_id":"850808447003656242","content":"*A handwritten note in neat writing reads:*\n\nLady Sabrine Lovlatar, a minor noble ousted from her land by the Redcoats in an event that left her disfigured and unable to speak, came to Empire City with nothing in order to seek treatment for her condition. She communicates through the imp-spirit Kukudh which guides her, and the strange psychic powers that manifested after the incident. While she may not have possessions, she has an odd wisdom about her, which she is willing to share if need be.\n\n\n...or at least... that's what she tells people. In reality---\n\n*The paper is torn here, the rest is illegible.*\n\n<https://www.dndbeyond.com/profile/DemifiendCruithne/characters/52815806>","created_at":"2021-07-10T17:54:13.266000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-10T17:54:37.664000Z","id":"863478232452300811","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
